\section*{1. Introduction}
The Continuous Yield Propulsion Core (CYPC-1) is a propulsion architecture
derived from the ACE-9K conservation engine. CYPC-1 converts controlled
information-density pressure fields into directed thrust while maintaining
structural, dynamical, and topological stability. This chapter defines the
engineering schematic, subsystem interactions, governing equations, and
stability constraints.

\section*{2. System Block Architecture}
CYPC-1 consists of four integrated subsystems:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item QP-Core: Pressure generation via information-density gradients
    \item SRK: Structural resistance and yield control
    \item FDE: Force propagation and thrust vectoring
    \item SFM: Global stability and manifold integrity
\end{enumerate}

The propulsion pipeline operates in Continuous Yield Mode (CYM), ensuring
bounded thrust generation under extreme gradients.

\section*{3. QP-Core Schematic (Pressure Generation)}
\subsection*{3.1 Governing Equations}
Pressure field:
\[
P(x) = \nabla \rho(x),
\]
Gradient coupling:
\[
\Gamma_P = \frac{\partial}{\partial x^\mu}\log\rho(x^\mu).
\]

\subsection*{3.2 Engineering Role}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Plasma/fuel intake encoded as $\rho(x)$
    \item Pressure chamber geometry shapes $\nabla\rho(x)$
    \item $\Gamma_P$ defines coupling into downstream thrust vectoring
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{3.3 Schematic Description}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Toroidal or cylindrical chamber
    \item Gradient coils for $\rho(x)$ shaping
    \item Pressure manifold feeding SRK boundary layer
\end{itemize}

\section*{4. SRK Schematic (Structural Resistance Kernel)}
\subsection*{4.1 Governing Equations}
Stress tensor:
\[
\sigma_{ij} = C_{ijkl}\epsilon_{kl},
\]
Yield function:
\[
f_{\text{yield}} = \sqrt{\sigma_{ij}\sigma^{ij}} - \sigma_{\text{crit}}.
\]

\subsection*{4.2 Engineering Role}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Defines thrust chamber material limits
    \item Maps deformation under thermal-mechanical loading
    \item Ensures $f_{\text{yield}} < 0$ during thrust cycles
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{4.3 Schematic Description}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Multi-layer composite hull
    \item Embedded strain-sensor lattice
    \item Adaptive geometry control for yield avoidance
\end{itemize}

\section*{5. FDE Schematic (Force Dynamics Engine)}
\subsection*{5.1 Governing Equations}
Dynamic thrust propagation:
\[
M\ddot{x}^\mu + D\dot{x}^\mu + Kx^\mu = F^\mu.
\]

\subsection*{5.2 Engineering Role}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Converts pressure field into thrust vector
    \item Damping matrix $D$ stabilizes oscillatory thrust modes
    \item Stiffness matrix $K$ defined by nozzle geometry and field coils
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{5.3 Schematic Description}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Magnetic-plasma nozzle
    \item Vectoring vanes or field coils
    \item Thrust manifold with dynamic stiffness control
\end{itemize}

\section*{6. SFM Schematic (Stability--Failure Manifold)}
\subsection*{6.1 Governing Equation}
Global stability condition:
\[
\lambda_{\max}(K - \Gamma_P) < 0.
\]

\subsection*{6.2 Engineering Role}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Ensures thrust generation remains globally stable
    \item Prevents manifold collapse under nozzle deformation
    \item Maintains topological integrity during high-gradient cycles
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{6.3 Schematic Description}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Stability sensor array
    \item Real-time eigenvalue spectrum evaluator
    \item Geometry modulation actuators
\end{itemize}

\section*{7. Conservation Layer Integration}
CYPC-1 inherits ACE-9K conservation constraints:
\[
\nabla_\mu T^{\mu\nu} = 0, \qquad 
\nabla_\mu J^\mu = 0,
\]
and preserves the invariant:
\[
\frac{dH_{\text{metric}}}{dt} \approx 0.
\]

\section*{8. Full Propulsion Pipeline Schematic}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Plasma/fuel intake $\rightarrow \rho(x)$ encoding
    \item Pressure generation via QP-Core
    \item Structural yield mapping via SRK
    \item Thrust propagation via FDE
    \item Stability evaluation via SFM
    \item Conservation and invariant validation
\end{enumerate}

\section*{9. Stability Envelope}
CYPC-1 stability envelope defined by:
\[
\lambda_{\max}(K - \Gamma_P) < 0,
\]
with observed propulsion-cycle value:
\[
\lambda_{\max} = -0.387.
\]

\section*{10. Engineering Notes}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Nozzle geometry must maintain negative eigenvalue spectrum
    \item Pressure chamber must avoid $\nabla\rho(x)$ runaway
    \item Damping matrix $D$ must remain positive definite
    \item Structural hull must maintain $f_{\text{yield}} < 0$
\end{itemize}

\section*{11. Conclusion}
The CYPC-1 propulsion core integrates ACE-9K physics into a stable,
high-gradient thrust engine. The schematic defined herein provides the
engineering foundation for implementation, optimization, and further
development of continuous-yield propulsion systems.

